# Milestone 34: the code block of a Markdown is the generated element Code block (reference/common/styles.md,
# reference/components/markdown.md). Page of 200 × 300 with margins of 20: page area of 160 × 260 from (20, 20).
# The line measures 120 % of the Size of its box.
#   md:   a Markdown with three blocks. "Antes." and "Después." are one-line Paragraph elements (Size 10: 12). The code
#         block is styled by For element: Code block (Size 5, Margin 4 0, Padding 5): two lines of 6 are 12 and with the
#         padding, 22. It goes between the two paragraphs with a margin of 4 above and below (the paragraphs have
#         no margin): 12 + 4 + 22 + 4 + 12 = 54. y = 20. For element: Text does not reach it: its Padding 3 would add 6.
#   t:    a normal Text: For element: Text gives it Padding 3, so it measures 12 + 6 = 18. y = 74.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 200
		Height: 300
		Margin: 20
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Mono
				Size: 10
		For element: Text
			Box:
				Padding: 3
		For element: Code block
			Typography:
				Size: 5
			Box:
				Margin: 4 0
				Padding: 5
				Background: #EEEEEE
	Section:
		Markdown:
			Id: md
			Typography:
				Code font: IBM Plex Mono
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
			Content >>
				Antes.

				```
				a  b
				  c
				```

				Después.
		Text: Hola
			Id: t
